  "configuration_id": "config_018",
  "reason": "Evidence: RNA-only with multiprofile+avgpool (config_002, acc=0.591) is the clear best so far, while image-only is very weak (config_010, acc=0.208). We also know avgpool > transformer for aggregation. The critical open question is whether the image modality provides any complementary signal when combined with the strong RNA features, which is the central premise of this multimodal study. Config_018 (multimodal, multiprofile, pca_n2000, resnet50, avgpool, concat) is the most direct logical extension of our best result: it keeps the proven RNA setup (multiprofile + avgpool + pca_n2000) and adds the image branch with the simplest standard fusion (concat). If it beats 0.591, multimodal fusion is validated and we can explore weighted fusion and better image encoders; if it does not, we learn that image adds no value and can redirect budget toward RNA encoder improvements (scvi/scgpt). This single experiment resolves the highest-uncertainty design decision under the limited budget."
}

